<p>Retrieves a local integer variable stored on an object.
</p>
<div class="dascript" style="font-family:monospace; background-color:#F9F9F9; border: 1px dashed #2F6FAB; white-space:pre; line-height:1.25em; padding:1.0em;"><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Int%20keyword" title="Int keyword">int</a> GetLocalInt(<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Object%20keyword" title="Object keyword">object</a> oObject,<br />    <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/String%20keyword" title="String keyword">string</a> sVarName<br />);</div>
<dl>
<dt>Parameters:
<dd><dl><dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">oObject<dd>The Object the variable is stored on<dt style="font-weight:normal; font-style:italic;">sVarName<dd>The name of the integer variable to retrieve
</dl>
</dl><dl><dt>Returns:
<p><dd>Returns the value of the integer variable. Returns 0 on error.
</p>
</dl><dl><dt>Source:
<p><dd><a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/Script.ldf" title="Script.ldf">script.ldf</a>
</p>
</dl>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Description">Description</span></h2>
<p>Returns the value of the integer variable with the name sVarName which is stored on the object oObject. If no such variable is stored on the object oObject, 0 is returned. 
</p><p>To change the value of a local integer value, use <a href="https://github.com/adarec1994/DragonAgeToolset/wiki/SetLocalInt" title="SetLocalInt">SetLocalInt</a>.
</p>
<h2><span class="mw-headline" id="Remarks">Remarks</span></h2>
<p>All local variables must be predefined in the target object's variables 2da file before this function can be used successfully. If a local variable is not predefined this function will fail silently.
</p>
